      "text": "On the asymptotic expansion of the Kashaev invariant of the 5 2 knot Tomotada Ohtsuki — We give a presentation of the asymptotic expansion of the Kashaev invariant of the 5 2 knot.\n\n**On the asymptotic expansion of the Kashaev invariant of the 5 2 knot Tomotada Ohtsuki**\n\n52 pp, 18 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We give a presentation of the asymptotic expansion of the Kashaev invariant of the 5 2 knot. As the volume conjecture states, the leading term of the expansion presents the hyperbolic volume and the Chern-Simons invariant of the complement of the 5 2 knot. Further, we obtain a method to compute the full Poincare asymptotics to all orders of the Kashaev invariant of the 5 2 knot.\n\n**Outline.** Abstract; 1 Introduction; 2 Calculation of the Kashaev invariant of the ; 2.2 Calculation of ⟨ 52 ⟩N toward its asymptot; 3 Calculation by the saddle point method; 2 (Nx 2)2 +b4Nx 2); 4 Calculation by the Poisson summation formula; 2 Re 1; 5 Proof of Theorem 1.1; 4.6 (Poisson summation formula) (see also Rema; 5.2 Calculation of the asymptotic expansion; 24 (x2; 2 (t0 +s0)2 + 1; 2 (2\u0019; 5 (\u0000Vts)3 + 3; 5.3 Verifying the assumption of the saddle poi; 5.4 Verifying the assumption of the Poisson su; References\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 1.1: The asymptotic expansion of the Kashaev invariant ⟨ 52 ⟩N of the 52 knot\n- Proposition 3.2: , and multi-variable cases in Propositions 3.4 and 3.5. We use Proposition\n- Proposition 3.1: For a non-zero a 2 C, the domain fz 2 C j Reaz2 < 0g has two\n- Proposition 3.2: Let a be a non-zero complex number, and let (z) and r(z) be holo-\n- Proposition 3.1: We put ^ r(z) = r(z)=z2. Since ^r(z) is analytic in a neighborhood of 0,\n- Proposition 3.1: , and obtain the second equality putting y =",
